ibaldi</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Popkave</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bylsma</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Career plans for trainees in internal medicine residency programs</article-title><source>Acad Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>507</fpage><lpage>512</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00001888-200505000-00021</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Garibaldi RA, Popkave C, Bylsma W. Career plans for trainees in internal medicine residency programs. Acad Med. 2005;80:507&#x02013;12. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15851467</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Larson</surname><given-names>EB</given-names></name><collab>the Society of General Internal Medicine (SGIM) Task Force on the Domain of General Internal Medicine</collab></person-group><article-title>Health care system chaos should spur innovation: summary of a report of the Society of General Internal Medicine Task Force on the Domain of General Internal Medicine</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>140</volume><fpage>639</fpage><lpage>643</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Larson EB, the Society of General Internal Medicine (SGIM) Task Force on the Domain of General Internal Medicine. Health care system chaos should spur innovation: summary of a report of the Society of General Internal Medicine Task Force on the Domain of General Internal Medicine. Ann Intern Med. 2004;140:639&#x02013;43. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15096335</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lambert</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Holmboe</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The relationship between specialty choice and gender of U.S. medical graduates</article-title><source>Acad Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>797</fpage><lpage>802</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00001888-200509000-00003</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Lambert EM, Holmboe ES. The relationship between specialty choice and gender of U.S. medical graduates. Acad Med. 2005;80:797&#x02013;802. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16123456</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blendon</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Schoen</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Donelan</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Osborn</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>DesRoches</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Scoles</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Physicians&#x02019; views on quality of care: a five-country comparison</article-title><source>Health Aff (Millwood)</source><year>2001</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>233</fpage><lpage>243</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1377/hlthaff.20.3.233</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Blendon RJ, Schoen C, Donelan K, Osborn R, DesRoches CM, Scoles K, et al. Physicians&#x02019; views on quality of care: a five-country comparison. Health Aff (Millwood). 2001;20:233&#x02013;43. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11585172</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mechanic</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Physician discontent: challenges and opportunities</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>2003</year><volume>290</volume><fpage>941</fpage><lpage>946</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.290.7.941</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Mechanic D. Physician discontent: challenges and opportunities. JAMA. 2003;290:941&#x02013;6. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12928472</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kassirer</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Doctor discontent</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>1998</year><volume>339</volume><fpage>1543</fpage><lpage>1545</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1056/NEJM199811193392109</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Kassirer JP. Doctor discontent. N Engl J Med. 1998;339:1543&#x02013;5. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9819454</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grumbach</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Primary care in the United States&#x02014;the best of times, the worst of times</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>1999</year><volume>341</volume><fpage>2008</fpage><lpage>2010</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1056/NEJM199912233412611</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Grumbach K. Primary care in the United States&#x02014;the best of times, the worst of times. N Engl J Med. 1999;341:2008&#x02013;10. Editorial. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10607821</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Showstack</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lurie</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Larson</surname><given-names>EB</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Primary care: the ne